# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
nothingness	one
migration	one
death_good	one
dreamless_best	one
one_night	one
# death_good: the nothingness branch (C1, through A1) grounds the gain in an absence of disturbance. P4 grounds it in the positive goods of the other world.
# Those are different reasons for the same verdict, that death is better for the one who dies than the alternative. They are not two meanings of "good".
# Nor does P4 contradict A1, since each conditional gets there from its own antecedent. I was unsure here but kept it as one.
# dreamless_best: one might object that a dreamless sleep is "pleasant" only in retrospect, which sits uneasily with "utter unconsciousness".
# That is a question about whether P2 is true. P2 and A1 use the claim in the same sense, so it is not a shift between statements.
